-- ako/mxcli#512 — "On click" on a List View (and on the two legacy image
-- widgets) was parsed, accepted, and dropped on write.
--
-- Before the fix, `mxcli check` said so honestly:
--
--     ⚠ widget `lvClick` (listview) has an on-click action, and Mendix does model
--       one on listview — but mxcli has no writer for it, so the value is dropped
--       and the widget does nothing                              [MDL-WIDGET23]
--       → Wrap the clickable part in a `container` and put the action there
--
-- Honest, and still a tool gap the author had to model around.
--
-- It turned out to be one line per widget. The MODEL already carried the field
-- (pages.ListView.ClickAction, pages.StaticImage/DynamicImage.OnClickAction) and
-- the WRITERS already serialised it — widget_write.go calls
-- clientActionToGen(x.ClickAction) for the list view, widget_write_legacy_gaps.go
-- does the same for both images. Only the builders never read the action off the
-- AST, so the field was always nil.
--
-- Measured on a blank Mendix 11.12.2 project:
--
--     exec      -> Created page MyFirstModule.OnClick
--     mx check  -> The app contains: 0 errors.
--     describe  -> listview lvClick (DataSource: …, Action: microflow …)
--     re-exec   -> Unchanged page      <- the describe output rebuilds the
--                                         stored document exactly
--
-- The describe half is not optional. The write half landed on its own first and
-- the action vanished on the next describe → exec: valid BSON, clean build,
-- construct silently gone — the half-shell trap this repo keeps recording.
-- Adding the emitter also duplicated `Editable: true` on every list view, which
-- only showed up by round-tripping a DIFFERENT page than the one under test.

create entity MyFirstModule.Thing ( Name: string(200) );
create microflow MyFirstModule.ACT_Nothing()
begin
  show message 'hi';
end;

create or replace page MyFirstModule.OnClick (
  title: 'c', layout: 'Atlas_Core.Atlas_Default'
) {
  listview lvClick (
    DataSource: database from MyFirstModule.Thing,
    Action: microflow MyFirstModule.ACT_Nothing
  ) {
    dynamictext dt (Content: 'x')
  }
};

-- The control that keeps the rule alive: Mendix models NO click action on a data
-- view, so MDL-WIDGET23 must still report this one. Emptying the rule's map
-- rather than correcting it would silence a real gap.
--
--   dataview dv (DataSource: microflow MyFirstModule.ACT_Nothing,
--                OnClick: microflow MyFirstModule.ACT_Nothing) { … }
--   -> MDL-WIDGET23: … Mendix models no click action on dataview at all
